--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Third-party notices
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

This repository vendors third-party projects under third_party/ for research and
host-side tooling. They are not part of the DSPMark.3dsx binary.

* Teakra (https://github.com/wwylele/teakra) — MIT License.
  Used as the instruction encoder (tools/teaasm), the emulator behind
  tools/dspsim, the disassembler behind tools/teacan, and as documentation for
  the XpertTeak peripherals.

* OpenDSP (https://github.com/Cellenseres/OpenDSP) — BSD 2-Clause License.
  Used as a reference for hardware-tested APBP, MIU and DMA register sequences
  and for the DSP firmware boot/unload protocol. No OpenDSP source is copied
  into the shipped component; the constants and protocol are re-implemented and
  credited in HARDWARE_NOTES.md.

DSPMark links against libctru (zlib) and, in future GPU work, citro3d (zlib).
No Nintendo firmware or proprietary code is included. The DSP component is an
original work assembled from dsp/*.asm.

Luma3DS was consulted to confirm which CFW properties are required (DSP
signature check patch and DSP RAM mapping for homebrew). No Luma3DS code is
included; Luma3DS is GPLv3.
